Contract correction from the WT-S revision after QA reject 1. Where this comment and the row's description differ, the revised docs/plans/2026-10-30-per-task-worktrees.md and this comment win. Section numbers are unchanged. Plan against revised §1.4 and §1.6:
1. The `.moe/` guard now FAILS CLOSED. This replaces "Warn MOE_WORKTREE_MOE_PRESENT if W/.moe exists", which rail 3 forbids. If `W/.moe` exists after create or reuse (a link counts):
   - print MOE_WORKTREE_MOE_PRESENT;
   - launch no CLI;
   - delete nothing and commit nothing, including no §3.3 recovery checkpoint;
   - call report_blocked with the code.
   Required negative case in postflight.{sh,ps1}: pre-create `W/.moe/x`, then assert that no CLI launched, `W/.moe/x` is still there, moe/task/<id> has no new commit, and report_blocked carried the code.
2. Add `--no-track` to `git worktree add … -b moe/task/<taskId>`.
3. Cutting W from the local target is still right for this slice. WT-09 switches the remote-mode base to refs/remotes/origin/<target> after its fetch (§1.2).
Everything else in the row is unchanged.
